logs
# Runtime data must never enter the build context. Patterns like `data/*.db`
# are not enough: Docker's ignore matching does not let `*` cross a `/`, so
# data/test/*.db, data/backups/**/*.db and data/logs/*.jsonl still matched.
# The database holds password hashes, raw session tokens and credential
# ciphertext; logs can hold streaming keys.
#
# Re-include only the bundled read-only assets the runtime image ships. A file
# cannot be re-included while its parent directory stays excluded, so each
# directory is restored explicitly, and the user-writable `custom` dirs are
# re-excluded after the broad `**` re-include (last match wins).
data/**
!data/indexers
!data/indexers/**
data/indexers/definitions/custom
!data/external-lists
!data/external-lists/**
data/external-lists/presets/custom
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
.DS_Store
